    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45819" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφολκ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drawing on, enticing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφολκὰ λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.108
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδὸς ἐφολκόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					291
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εἰς παρρησίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					8.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσα κυνὶ ὀρέγεται ἐ. εἰς τὴν
					ἑαντοῦ φιλίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>NA</u>
					7.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>requiring to be drawn on, laggard</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				268
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ πρόλεσχος μηδ᾽ ἐ. ἐν
			λόγῳ</span> not eager to begin, nor yet <i>lagging,
			tedious</i> in reply, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				200
			</span></i>.</div>
